    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105240" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίσ-μᾰκαρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰρος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, strengthd.
		for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάκαρ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thrice-blest,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				6.154
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				155
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1332
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.254.17
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.), etc.:—the divided form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς μάκαρ</span> is supported by the phrase
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς μάκαρες καὶ τετράκις</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.306
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισμάκαρες</span> codd.), cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				81.7
			</span></i> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισμακάριστος.</span></div>
